Correction: this message says the handoff "is injected on every turn". It is
not. The handoff block is sent at session start and after a compaction only
(flows.py, `is_new or reinject.take(key)`), and the appended system prompt is
set per CLI call, so nothing carries it between those boundaries.

The history itself works as described. What was wrong was the reason given for
keeping it small, and the implication that a pointer sent inside the handoff
block would still be in front of the model on a later turn. Fixed in 8837787,
which sends the pointer on every turn and corrects the README.
